IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: Writ Petition (Civil) No. 55 of 2023
CITATION: 2023 SCC OnLine SC 1348
YEAR: 2023

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: D.Y. Chandrachud, S.K. Kaul, S. Ravindra Bhat, Hima Kohli, P.S. Narasimha

PARTIES:
Supriyo vs Union of India

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Special Marriage Act, 1954, Constitution of India

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Article 14, Article 19, Article 21

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
same-sex marriage, special marriage act, legislative domain, civil unions

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Held that there is no unqualified fundamental right to marry, leaving the legal recognition of marriage for queer couples to the competence of Parliament.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Article 14, Article 19, Article 21.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

